---
import LegalDoc from "../components/LegalDoc.astro";
import { COMPANY, CONTACT_EMAIL, EFFECTIVE } from "../data/legal";
const glance = [
	"videomk turns what you type or say (and photos you choose) into a narrated video.",
	"Your prompts, photos and videos are private to your account. We do not use them to train AI models, and we do not sell personal data.",
	"We show no ads and use no advertising or analytics trackers in the app.",
	"To make a video we send your text (and photos you attach) to AI and media services that work for us. Section 4 lists them.",
	"Your photos are cleaned of all hidden data (location, camera, date) before they are stored, and the originals are deleted. If you allow it in Settings, the time each photo was taken and an approximate place (about 1 km) are used once to tell your story; the place is turned into a city name on our servers and the coordinates are not kept.",
	"My media (optional): you can keep your photos in a private library in videomk and search them by describing them. Only you can see them; nobody at videomk browses them. You can delete any photo, or all of them, at any time in the app.",
	"You can ask us to delete your videos or your whole account at any time.",
];
const sections = [
	{ title: "Who we are", paras: [
		`This policy explains how ${COMPANY} (“videomk”, “we”, “us”) processes personal data when you use the videomk apps for iPhone and Android, and the videomk website. ${COMPANY} is the controller of that data.`,
		"It covers what we collect, why, who receives it, how long we keep it and your rights, including under the UK GDPR and the EU GDPR where they apply."] },
	{ title: "What we collect", paras: ["Depending on how you use videomk:"], bullets: [
		"Account data: your email address and an account identifier. You sign in with email and a password, handled by Amazon Cognito. We never see your password in readable form.",
		"What you ask for: the text of your requests (typed, or dictated and turned into text), the options you choose (length, look, subtitles, language), and any edits you make to a video.",
		"Photos you attach: up to 100 per video. Before upload, your phone removes all metadata from the photo file (location, camera and date) and resizes it.",
		"Photo date and approximate location (optional): if the two switches in Settings are on (they are on by default), the phone also reads when each photo was taken and where, from the photo's own data, and sends the date and time and a location rounded to about 1 km with your request, never inside the photo. We use them to put your photos in order, group them by day and name the places in your story. The location is turned into a place name from public map data on our own servers (no other company receives it); the coordinates are discarded as soon as the story is planned, while the place name and the time stay with your video. Turn the switches off and none of this is read or sent.",
		"Photos you keep in My media (optional): the photos you choose to add to your library, a small preview of each, the date it was taken and the name of the place (city and country) if you allowed those in Settings, the collections you create, and a numerical “fingerprint” of each photo that lets you find it by describing it. We do not store the exact coordinates, and your photos are cleaned of hidden data on your phone before they are uploaded.",
		"What you search for in My media: the words you type to find your photos. They are used only to answer that search.",
		"What we make for you: the script, narration audio, the finished video and the list of sources and credits shown with it.",
		"Credits and purchases: your credit balance and history. Payments are handled by Apple or Google; we receive confirmation of a purchase, never your card details.",
		"Technical data: IP address, device type and app version, time of each request, and error logs. This is used for security, abuse prevention and fixing faults.",
		"Messages you send us when you contact support."] },
	{ title: "How we use it", paras: ["We use personal data to:"], bullets: [
		"create the videos you ask for, keep them in your library, and let you edit, play and share them;",
		"keep your account secure, limit abuse (for example repeated free sign-ups) and keep the service running and fast;",
		"count and give you credits, process purchases and refunds;",
		"answer your questions and tell you about important changes to the service;",
		"meet legal obligations and defend legal claims."] },
	{ title: "Who receives your data (our service providers)", paras: [
		"We use these providers to run videomk. Each receives only what it needs for its part, and none may use it for its own advertising or to train its own models.",
	], bullets: [
		"Amazon Web Services: hosting, storage, sign-in (Cognito), and the AI models and voices we use through Amazon Bedrock and Amazon Polly. Your text and photos are processed inside our AWS account; Amazon states that Bedrock does not use your inputs to train models or share them with model providers. Servers are in Ireland and the United States.",
		"Anthropic’s Claude models (through Amazon Bedrock): write the script and review photos and clips.",
		"Tavily: for topics that need current information, short search queries about your topic (not your name, email or photos) are sent to a web search service, and the pages found are read to write an accurate script.",
		"Stock photo and video libraries (Unsplash, Openverse, Pixabay, Pexels, Wikimedia Commons): our servers send search words for the pictures and clips a scene needs. They do not receive your account details or your own photos.",
		"Apple and Google: sign-in is by email, but app distribution, in-app purchases and (optionally) speech recognition are provided by Apple’s and Google’s own services under their policies.",
		"Professional advisers, and authorities where the law requires, or a buyer if our business is sold, under confidentiality.",
		"We do not sell personal data and do not share it for advertising."] },
	{ title: "Photos and AI processing", paras: [
		"Photos you attach are checked by an AI model so the video can describe them and so unsafe images are refused. To keep this cheap and private, the photos are shown to the model as small numbered thumbnails, ten to a sheet, and the story is then worked out from the descriptions alone. The location, camera and date data are removed from the photo file on your phone, and again on our servers. We delete the original upload as soon as the cleaned copy is made (any leftover is removed automatically within 2 days).",
		"The cleaned copy stays with the video it belongs to, because editing needs it, until that video is deleted.",
		"Videos are made by AI and may contain mistakes. They are labelled as made with AI where the app or store requires it."] },
	{ title: "My media: your private photo library", paras: [
		"My media is optional. If you add photos to it, we store them privately in our cloud storage under your account, encrypted, until you delete them or your account. Only you can see them: every request is checked against your signed-in account, links to your photos are short-lived and can only be created for you, and nobody at videomk browses your library.",
		"To let you find photos by describing them (for example “my holidays in Thailand in 2024”), each photo is turned into a numerical fingerprint by an AI model of Amazon Bedrock inside our own AWS account, and your search words are turned into one the same way; a small language model also reads your search words to pick out dates and places that exist in your own library. The photos and the words are not sent to any other company and are not used to train models.",
		"When you choose photos from My media for a video, they are copied into that video like photos you attach from your phone, and are handled as described in the section above.",
		"Deleting a photo removes the photo, its preview, its fingerprint and its record. “Delete everything” and deleting your account remove your whole library. Free accounts have a storage limit; if a paid plan ends, nothing is deleted, but you cannot add photos until you are under the limit, and you can still view and delete them."] },
	{ title: "Voice input", paras: [
		"Dictation is optional. The microphone is used only while you press the microphone button. Your phone’s own speech recognition turns your voice into text: on iPhone this is done by Apple (on the device when possible, otherwise on Apple’s servers) and on Android by Google’s speech service. We receive only the text, never the audio. How Apple and Google treat audio is described in their policies."] },
	{ title: "No training on your content", paras: [
		"We do not use your prompts, photos, narration or videos to train or fine-tune AI models, and our providers listed above are not permitted to use them to train theirs."] },
	{ title: "How long we keep data", bullets: [
		"Videos, narration, photos you attached and the plan behind each video: until you delete them or your account.",
		"Photos in My media, their previews, fingerprints and collections: until you delete them or your account.",
		"Temporary working files used to build a video: automatically deleted after 7 days.",
		"Safety checks: your description is checked by an AI model for safety before a video is made. If a request is stopped, we keep the type of reason, the time, a short excerpt (up to 160 characters) and a fingerprint of the request for 90 days, to review mistakes and spot repeated misuse; requests that pass leave no record.",
		"Upload leftovers: deleted within 2 days. Technical and error logs: deleted after 14 days.",
		"Account, credit and purchase records: while your account exists, then only as long as the law requires (for example accounting records).",
		"Backups and provider caches are overwritten on their normal cycles."] },
	{ title: "Sharing a video", paras: [
		"If you share a video link, anyone with the link can watch it without signing in, and we cannot control where the link travels or whether it is copied. Share only what you are happy to be public."] },
	{ title: "Your rights and deleting your data", paras: [
		"Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to our use of your data, to receive a copy of it, and to withdraw consent. You may also complain to your data protection authority (in the UK, the Information Commissioner’s Office).",
		`To use these rights, or to delete your videos or your whole account and everything linked to it, email ${CONTACT_EMAIL} from the address on your account. See also videomk.com/delete-account. We answer within 30 days, and we may need to confirm it is you.`] },
	{ title: "Where data is processed", paras: [
		"Data may be processed in the United Kingdom, the European Economic Area, the United States and other countries where our providers operate. Where required we rely on adequacy decisions, standard contractual clauses or equivalent safeguards."] },
	{ title: "Security", paras: [
		"Connections are encrypted, storage is private to our accounts, access to videos uses short-lived links, and we limit who can access production data. No system is perfectly secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security."] },
	{ title: "Children", paras: [
		"videomk is for people aged 13 and over. It is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect data from them. If you think a child has given us data, contact us and we will delete it."] },
	{ title: "Cookies on the website", paras: [
		"The website uses only what is needed to keep you signed in. It sets no advertising or analytics cookies."] },
	{ title: "Changes", paras: [
		"We may update this policy. We will change the date at the top and, where the law requires, tell you in the app or by email."] },
	{ title: "Contact", paras: [`Questions or requests: ${CONTACT_EMAIL}. ${COMPANY} is responsible for videomk for the purposes of this policy.`] },
];
---
<LegalDoc title="Privacy Policy" intro="How videomk handles your data: what we collect, why, who helps us, how long we keep it and how to delete it." effective={EFFECTIVE} glance={glance} sections={sections} />
